<% content_for :title, "Popover" %>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Overlays</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Popover</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    A panel of rich content anchored to a button: a record's details, a short form, a set of actions. It paints above
    everything, closes when you click outside or press Escape, moves focus in when it opens and back to the button when it
    closes, and stays on screen near a viewport edge. There's nothing Rails-specific in it — it earns its place because
    that behaviour is hard to get right.
  </p>
</div>

<%# Preview %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background flex items-center justify-center gap-6 p-12 mb-8">
  <%= render Ui::PopoverComponent.new(placement: :bottom) do |p| %>
    <% p.with_trigger do %>
      <button class="rounded-md bg-primary px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors">
        Open popover
      </button>
    <% end %>
    <% p.with_panel(class: "w-64 p-4") do %>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1">Popover title</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">Rich HTML content — any markup goes here.</p>
      <div class="flex gap-2">
        <button class="rounded px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90">Confirm</button>
        <button class="rounded px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium border border-input hover:bg-accent hover:text-accent-foreground">Cancel</button>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# Usage %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800 mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#popover-usage" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed"><code id="popover-usage" class="text-neutral-200"><%= h(example_popover_usage) %></code></pre>
</div>

<%# Options %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Options</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Name</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Type</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Default</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["placement",    "String or Symbol", '"bottom"', "One of the 12 placements: top, top-start, top-end, bottom, … right-end. :bottom_start works as well as \"bottom-start\"."],
        ["offset",       "Integer", "8",        "Gap in pixels between the trigger and the panel."],
        ["class",        "String",  "nil",      "Merged onto the popover's root element, which wraps the trigger. Style the panel through the panel slot's class: instead."],
        ["panel_classes","String",  "nil",      "Deprecated: pass the classes to with_panel(class:), which merges them the same way. Removed in 0.4.0."],
      ].each do |name, type, default, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= name %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= type %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><%= default %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# Slots %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Slots</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Name</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <tr>
        <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary">trigger</td>
        <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground">The button or element that toggles the panel open/closed.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary">panel</td>
        <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground">The floating panel content. Any HTML — links, forms, text, actions. <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">with_panel(class: "w-64 p-4")</code> merges classes over the panel's own with tailwind_merge, so <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">bg-muted</code> replaces its background rather than racing it.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# Accessibility %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Accessibility</h2>
<ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2 mb-8 list-disc ps-5">
  <li>The button in the trigger slot gets <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-expanded</code>, <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-haspopup="dialog"</code> and
      <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-controls</code>, kept in step as the panel opens and closes.</li>
  <li>Focus moves into the panel when it opens and returns to the button when it closes — unless the click that dismissed
      it moved focus somewhere else on purpose.</li>
  <li>Escape closes the topmost popover, whatever has focus inside it.</li>
  <li>The trigger must be a real button, so it can be reached and pressed from the keyboard.</li>
</ul>

<%# Not this %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">When not to use it</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-8">
  A short text hint is a <%= link_to "Tooltip", tooltip_path, class: "text-primary underline" %>. A list of actions is a
  <%= link_to "Dropdown", dropdown_path, class: "text-primary underline" %> menu, with its keyboard model. Anything that needs the
  user's full attention, or a form longer than a couple of fields, is a <%= link_to "Modal", modal_path, class: "text-primary underline" %>.
</p>
